        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It's mainly for 'neovide' and maybe for other plugins that provide visual feedback when cursor jumps. In 'neovide' there's a visual effect for when cursor jumps and it can be distracting in this particular case because cursor jumps in cmdline only to be 'hidden'. That's why I think it would be better if 'mini.pick' truly hid cursor.\r\n\r\nI see. I'll take a look, but in my experience this type of \"cache and restore\" is better to be avoided because if something goes wrong (in this case, `MiniPickStop` `User` event is not triggered for some reason), cursor might not get restored. And this will be a very visible (or, rather, invisible :) ) issue.",
